enum StringRangeMethod { | engine Slice Substring Substr SingleIndex SingleRelativeIndex }
enum RegExpMatchForm { | engine Test Exec Search Match }
flags PropertyDescriptorFlags { | engine HasValue HasWritable IsWritable HasEnumerable IsEnumerable HasConfigurable IsConfigurable HasGet HasSet }
# What the walk knows of the lists of a call in line of the family ArrayBuiltin, where the call has its last operands. The emitters of the family read it through InlineCall (codegen/AOTInlineCall.h) and ask Facts only where it says Other.
# storageOfReceiver: the kind of storage that the receiver is PROVEN to have wherever the call may be built: by Link, by the allocation, or by a test behind which the name of the receiver stands. Never Double for a list that may have Int32 storage in its place. Other: nobody has said.
# storageOfFirstList and the two behind it: the same of the first three arguments. storageOfResult: the one kind that Facts names for every array that the call makes. ReceiverKeepsStorage: Link has decided that the lists which the receiver may be keep their kind.
# ReceiverStaysEmpty: nothing is ever stored into the receiver. ElementsAreStrings: nothing but strings. Expects..: what the elements are expected to be says which kinds get an arm. Each arm stands behind the test of its kind.
# SomeResultKeepsStorage: Facts has decided the kind of some array that the call makes, which is then read without a test. ResultGetsNames: somewhere the program stores under a name into an array that the call makes.
flags FactsOfLists { | engine ReceiverKeepsStorage ReceiverStaysEmpty ElementsAreStrings ExpectsNoElements ExpectsAnything ExpectsInt32s ExpectsDoubles ExpectsValues SomeResultKeepsStorage ResultGetsNames }
parameters ListStamp (engine storageOfReceiver: ArrayStorage, engine storageOfResult: ArrayStorage, engine storageOfFirstList: ArrayStorage, engine storageOfSecondList: ArrayStorage, engine storageOfThirdList: ArrayStorage, engine factsOfLists: FactsOfLists)

